ors.v1"/><atom:link href="/sap/bc/adt/rap/generators/ui/webapi-service/tabl/$sideeffect" rel="http://www.sap.com/adt/serverdriven/sideeffect" type="application/vnd.sap.adt.serverdriven.sideeffects.result.v1+xml"/><atom:published>2024-04-02T00:00:00Z</atom:published><atom:summary>This generator creates all the repository objects that are relevant for a business object and for a RAP Web API service.The end result is a full-blown RAP Web API Service.Web APIs can be consumed by any OData client. A Web API service does not provide any UI-specific information in the service metadata. Specifically, the following repository objects are created: &lt;li&gt;SAP object node type&lt;/li&gt;  &lt;li&gt;SAP object type&lt;/li&gt;  &lt;li&gt;Service binding&lt;/li&gt;  &lt;li&gt;Service definition &lt;/li&gt;  &lt;li&gt;Access control &lt;/li&gt;  &lt;li&gt;RAP projection behavior definition &lt;/li&gt;  &lt;li&gt;RAP behavior definition &lt;/li&gt;  &lt;li&gt;Data definition for CDS projection view entity &lt;/li&gt;  &lt;li&gt;Data definition for CDS view entity &lt;/li&gt;  &lt;li&gt;ABAP class for ABAP behavior pool &lt;/li&gt; </atom:summary><atom:title>OData-Web-API-Service</atom:title><atom:updated>2024-04-02T00:00:00Z</atom:updated></atom:entry></atom:feed>
